  "question": "with the SEED as the replication unit, can this dataset distinguish each K-curve arm from the K=1 anchor?",
  "why": "kcurve_report.py pairs on the test trajectory with seeds averaged into the point estimate, so its p-values do not carry seed uncertainty and are conservative for arms with fewer seeds than the anchor -- conservative in the direction that manufactures 'indistinguishable'",
